  "description": "For a truly great mixed greens salad, make your own mix with the freshest stuff you can find: whole heads of lettuce, radicchio, herbs, dandelion greens, and more.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: wild leafy greens and tender fresh herbs → cultivated leafy greens and tender fresh herbs; Kosher salt → sea salt\n\nNotes: The key here is to use what you can get, and not try to force anything into the salad that won't be great. If you live near a farm stand or farmers market, that may be your best bet.If not, or if it's not the right season, stick to hardy leafy vegetables and herbs like radicchio, endive, romaine, escarole, frisée, and baby kale.",
